{"name":"Wind Chime","hex":"#dfe0e2","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"wind chime","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A set of decorative metallic or wooden tubular bells that sound when blown by the wind.","A singular tubular bell."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wind_chime"}],"entries":[{"title":"Wind chime","blocks":[{"text":"Wind chimes are a type of percussion instrument constructed from suspended tubes, rods, bells, or other objects that are often made of metal or wood. The tubes or rods are suspended along with some type of weight or surface which the tubes or rods can strike when they or another wind-catching surface are blown by the natural movement of air outside."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/Wchime.jpg/330px-Wchime.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wind_chime"},{"title":"Chime (musician)","blocks":[{"text":"Freya Goldfinch, also known by her stage name Chime, is a British electronic music producer and DJ. She is known for her work in the dubstep and bass music scenes, in particular the development of the colour bass subgenre. Chime coined the term \"colour bass\" to describe a style of dubstep with its focus on vibrant, bright and colourful production and sound design. Chime founded the record label Rushdown in 2016 to promote artists producing colour bass. Chime previously released music as part of Caution & Crisis and under the alias Dec3mber before adopting the alias Chime in 2015. Chime is transgender, having come out on August 2, 2026."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/1/15/Chime%28musician%29.png/330px-Chime%28musician%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chime_(musician)"},{"title":"Wind","blocks":[{"text":"Wind is the natural movement of air or other gases relative to a planet's surface. Winds occur on a range of scales, from thunderstorm flows lasting tens of minutes, to local breezes generated by heating of land surfaces and lasting a few hours, to global winds resulting from the difference in absorption of solar energy between the climate zones on Earth. The study of wind is known as anemology."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Cherry_tree_moving_in_the_wind_1.gif/330px-Cherry_tree_moving_in_the_wind_1.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wind"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Roman_wind_chime_%28tintinabulum%29_flying_phallus_with_bells.jpg/500px-Roman_wind_chime_%28tintinabulum%29_flying_phallus_with_bells.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Roman_wind_chime_%28tintinabulum%29_flying_phallus_with_bells.jpg/1280px-Roman_wind_chime_%28tintinabulum%29_flying_phallus_with_bells.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Roman_wind_chime_%28tintinabulum%29_flying_phallus_with_bells.jpg/500px-Roman_wind_chime_%28tintinabulum%29_flying_phallus_with_bells.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Bronze tintinnabulum, Roman, 1st century CE, British Museum.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARoman_wind_chime_(tintinabulum)_flying_phallus_with_bells.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/Wind-powered_bell_under_temple_eaves%2C._Banna-ji._Ashikaga%2C_Tochigi.jpg/500px-Wind-powered_bell_under_temple_eaves%2C._Banna-ji._Ashikaga%2C_Tochigi.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/Wind-powered_bell_under_temple_eaves%2C._Banna-ji._Ashikaga%2C_Tochigi.jpg/500px-Wind-powered_bell_under_temple_eaves%2C._Banna-ji._Ashikaga%2C_Tochigi.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Wind-powered bell or wind chime under temple eaves,. Banna-ji. Ashikaga, Tochigi. Japan","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWind-powered_bell_under_temple_eaves%2C._Banna-ji._Ashikaga%2C_Tochigi.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/Windglockenspiel.Koshi.jpg/250px-Windglockenspiel.Koshi.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/c4/Windglockenspiel.Koshi.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/Windglockenspiel.Koshi.jpg/250px-Windglockenspiel.Koshi.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Wind chime with the audible tones a1-d2-f2-g2-a2-d3-f3-a3. The bamboo cylinder is not only the case of the instrument, but at the same time it is the resonator. The eight tones are produced by eight metal rods within the cylinder which are centrally struck by a disk attached to the cord with the wind sail.  \n\n","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWindglockenspiel.Koshi.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/Chime_closeup.jpg/500px-Chime_closeup.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/Chime_closeup.jpg/500px-Chime_closeup.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A close-up of metal rods on a wind chime","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AChime_closeup.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/Free-Free_Euler-Bernoulli_Beam_animation.gif/330px-Free-Free_Euler-Bernoulli_Beam_animation.gif?utm_